  "evidence": "Moz Pro's pricing page sells flat plans with \"1 user included\" to \"3 users included\" and extra seats; the Help Hub describes adding colleagues only as invited Shared Users (seats) managed by the primary account holder, with no SSO or SCIM documented.",
  "notes": "Researched Moz Pro, Moz's main multi-user product (Moz Local, Moz API and STAT noted, not split). No SCIM by absence: pricing page, Moz Pro Enterprise page, Help Hub sitemap (302 articles) and API docs mention no SCIM, SAML SSO or provisioning. Flat pricing: Starter $49/month (individuals, single website), Standard $79/mo yearly (1 user), Medium $143/mo yearly (2 users), Large $239/mo yearly (3 users); additional seats $49/mo on any plan; Enterprise is Contact Sales. Okta's OIN app for Moz is password vaulting (SWA) only. The Moz API is an SEO data API, not a user-management API.",
